	(text_box "ADL5602: 50 Ohm matched input/output, 20 dB gain, DC to 4 GHz. 3-pin SOT-89 -- NO separate VCC pin.  DC bias enters through the RFOUT pin (pin 3) via bias tee inductor L5 .  This is standard for MMIC gain blocks.  L5 (RFC) feeds DC while presenting high impedance at RF.  Expected output: -7 dBm (tripler) + 20 dB (MMIC) ~~+13 dBm at 437 MHz.  May need an attenuator pad if output exceeds amateur power limits or if the MMIC saturates -- check P1dB in datasheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.93 162.0793 0)
		(size 68.58 18.2607)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "948c51c2-682e-419e-aaf5-4bfe0a77763c")
	)
	(text_box "TX CHAIN - 437 MHz BPSK downlink transmitter.  The carrier from the Si5351A (145.67 MHz) is BPSK-modulated by the 74LVC1G86 XOR gate, then frequency-tripled to 437 MHz by a class-C biased 2SC3356 transistor. A 2-pole cap-coupled Chebyshev BPF selects the 3rd harmonic and rejects the fundamental and 2nd harmonic.  The ADL5602 MMIC provides ~~20 dB gain to bring the signal to ~~+11.9 dBm output.  BPSK phase states are preserved through odd-order multiplication: 3 x 180* = 540* = 180*"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.93 55.88 0)
		(size 142.24 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b092de76-3009-4a59-a4eb-9c033b557f73")
	)
	(text_box "Class-C frequency tripler. R5 (47K Ohm) biases the transistor below cutoff -- it only conducts on positive input peaks, generating strong harmonic content.  47kOhm was empirically optimized on the breadboard prototype: -7.4 dBm at 437 MHz with 2N3904 (vs -12.2 dBm at 10kOhm). BRF92A (ft=5 GHz, SOT-23) is the flight transistor; 2N3904 (ft=300MHz) validated during bring-up.  RFC L1 provides DC bias path while presenting high impedance at RF.  SRF of L1 must be well above 437 MHz -- Coilcraft 0805CS-221XJRC (SRF ~\n.5GHz). Supply is +5V for maximum collector swing and harmonic output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 115.57 0)
		(size 53.34 28.4838)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b1d47c1b-551a-4baa-8f40-2ca6d243d9ba")
	)
	(text_box "437 MHz BPF: 2-pole capacitively-coupled Chebyshev (2 LC resonators +\n  series coupling cap + I/O coupling caps). Moderate bandwidth (~tens of MHz),\n  deliberately NOT narrow -- wide keeps IL low and holds 437 in-band despite\n  tuning/temperature drift. Target IL <2 dB at 437 (sim ~1.3 dB). Two of these\n  cascade: pre-MMIC and post-MMIC.\n\n  ALL capacitors MUST be C0G/NP0 dielectric -- X7R has voltage-dependent\n  capacitance that detunes the filter and generates intermodulation products\n  at RF.\n\n  Starting values -- tune with VNA during bring-up. Tune IN-CHAIN, not on a\n  50-ohm bench sweep: the tripler tank's source impedance shifts the center\n  (a 50-ohm sweep mis-predicts it). Resonator tuning pads add capacitance =\n  lower center (add-only direction).\n\n  Rejection at the antenna (full chain = both BPFs + collector tank):\n    145.67 MHz (fundamental)  >40 dB   (far out, easy)\n    291.3 MHz  (2nd harmonic)  >30 dB   (crushed, ~-69 dBc achieved)\n    582.7 MHz  (4th harmonic)  >20 dB   <- WATCH ITEM: the 2-pole's weak\n                                            high side (~-13 dB per stage,\n                                            ~-37 dBc in the full chain)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
